l functions with different bases never grow at the"},{"x":0.39203,"y":0.59643,"w":0.54655,"h":0.02323,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"same rate as x S q. If a 7 b 7 0, then ax grows faster than bx. Since (a>b) 7 1,"},{"x":0.63725,"y":0.6284,"w":0.0492,"h":0.03056,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"xSq aa"},{"x":0.67828,"y":0.6284,"w":0.01711,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"bb"},{"x":0.59965,"y":0.63021,"w":0.06261,"h":0.02869,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"ax bx = lim"},{"x":0.70933,"y":0.63688,"w":0.03565,"h":0.01475,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= q."},{"x":0.56914,"y":0.63884,"w":0.02833,"h":0.02012,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"lim xSq"},{"x":0.36261,"y":0.6663,"w":0.5881,"h":0.02882,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"(f) In contrast to exponential functions, logarithmic functions with different bases a 7 1 and b 7 1 always grow at the same rate as x S q:"},{"x":0.66132,"y":0.69355,"w":0.10724,"h":0.04173,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"ln x>ln a ln x>ln b = ln b"},{"x":0.57026,"y":0.70446,"w":0.08555,"h":0.03142,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"logax logbx = lim"},{"x":0.53975,"y":0.7143,"w":0.02833,"h":0.02012,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"lim xSq"},{"x":0.74363,"y":0.7143,"w":0.03072,"h":0.02008,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"ln a."},{"x":0.63081,"y":0.72372,"w":0.02833,"h":0.0107,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"xSq"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.74243,"w":0.35118,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The limiting ratio is always finite and never zero."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.77117,"w":0.58812,"h":0.0301,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"If ƒ grows at the same rate as g as x S q, and g grows at the same rate as h as x S q, then ƒ grows at the same rate as h as x S q. The reason is that"},{"x":0.73158,"y":0.81078,"w":0.04785,"h":0.02973,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"g h = L2"},{"x":0.56519,"y":0.81096,"w":0.16422,"h":0.02961,"fs":0.01279,"n":5,"k":1,"t":"ƒ g = L1 and lim xSq"},{"x":0.53468,"y":0.82045,"w":0.02833,"h":0.02012,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"lim xSq"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.8